374	 *
375	 * A present `primary` identity (immutable, e.g. `github_user_id`) is
376	 * authoritative: it governs even when it matches nothing (a new account), so a
377	 * stale non-primary like a reused `github_login` can't merge a fresh account
378	 * into the old person. Without a primary, identities match equal-weight (the
379	 * cross-channel behavior whatsapp/email rely on).
