382	 * resolution sites: the ordinary lookup AND the orphan-recovery re-resolution
383	 * after a lost auto-create race. Those two used to carry separate copies and the
384	 * recovery copy was tier-blind, which mis-resolved whenever a primary's owner
385	 * was soft-deleted while a live entity held a recycled secondary claim — the
386	 * link landed on the recycled-claim holder. `member_of` is a read ACL, so that
387	 * handed one person another person's channel access.
